  "_comment": "Quick check of a decode limit for leases on the 8-slot shared KV pool. Leasing 6 slots (lease_kvu8_c6, the best config so far) gave new-task TTFT P95 about +50% vs the main line, partly because new tasks wait for slots held over tool waits (~565 holds of ~1.2 s per run, about one slot idle on average). lease_kvu8_dec6 has 8 slots but admits new tasks only while fewer than 6 are busy decoding (held slots do not count), so the decode batch stays near 6, and only while the live tasks' estimated peak contexts fit the 24,576-token pool (leasing 8 at 1.15X filled it and 16 tasks failed). Seed 42 only, at 0.95X and 1.15X, each pair back to back. 4 runs, ~1.2 h. A screen, not a result: run the 3-seed sweep only if dec6 looks promising. Compare with: python -m analysis.paired results/phase2_lease_dec_quick --baseline lease_kvu8_c6 (pairs each load separately).",
